From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 08:52:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom: scm: Allow QSEECOM on the HP OmniBook 5

The OmniBook 5's tree carried the ThinkPad T14s compatible to get onto
this list, and its EFI variables worked that way. Give the laptop its
own entry instead. Without QSEECOM it has no EFI variables, so an
installer cannot write its boot entry.

Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index 61c1348..c756b55 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2319,6 +2319,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_scm_qseecom_allowlist[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "hp,elitebook-6-g1q" },
 	{ .compatible = "hp,elitebook-ultra-g1q" },
 	{ .compatible = "hp,elitebook-x-g2q" },
+	{ .compatible = "hp,omnibook-5" },
 	{ .compatible = "hp,omnibook-ultra-kg0xxx" },
 	{ .compatible = "hp,omnibook-x14" },
 	{ .compatible = "huawei,gaokun3" },
-- 
2.56.0

